Package: ForestFireR
Type: Package
Title: Spatial and Mean-Field Forest-Fire Invasion Model
Version: 0.9.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Leonardo A.", "Saravia", email = "lasaravia@untdf.edu.ar",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Rebeca", "de la Fuente", role = "aut"))
Description: Simulation of a two-species vegetation system in which fire
    mediates the competition between a native species and an invader.
    The same continuous-time transition rules are simulated on an explicit
    lattice with the Gillespie algorithm, as the deterministic well-mixed
    (mean-field) limit, and as the well-mixed stochastic process at a finite
    population size. Fire spread, post-fire regrowth and the clustering of
    the initial landscape are set through dimensionless parameters
    ('xi', 'eta', 'p'); landscape generators, trajectory and grid recording,
    fire-activity snapshots, animation rendering and reproducible seeding
    are provided. The simulation engine is written in C++ and exposed to R
    through 'Rcpp'. The model definition is documented in the package, under
    help("ForestFireR-model").
